l":null,"created_at":"2014-11-19T21:01:08Z","label":{"name":"Defect","color":"f7c6c7"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/comments/63715435","html_url":"https://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/issues/5211#issuecomment-63715435","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/5211","id":63715435,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDYzNzE1NDM1","user":{"login":"sdustinh","id":2855100,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTUxMDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2855100?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdustinh","html_url":"https://github.com/sdustinh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdustinh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdustinh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdustinh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdustinh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdustinh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdustinh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdustinh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdustinh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdustinh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2014-11-19T21:19:03Z","updated_at":"2014-11-19T21:19:03Z","body":"I was originally trying to do this...\n\n``` php\n$substring = $Query->func()->substring([$field => 'literal', 34]);\n$cast = $Query->func()->cast([$substring, ' AS SIGNED']);\n```\n\n... with the intention of `CAST(SUBSTRING(field, 34) AS SIGNED)` created. It isn't directly related to numeric values not being handled as literal so much as it is something that I stumbled across when updating some behaviors. The `FunctionExpression` forces a `,` as a conjunction. Now that I look at the [QueryExtension](https://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/blob/3.0/src/Database/Expression/QueryExpression.php#L81) class I see I could just call the `type()` method to overwrite it to a space. I think it was difficult to handle because I didn't read deep enough. :worried: \n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/comments/63715435/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"sdustinh","id":2855100,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTUxMDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2855100?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdustinh","html_url":"https://github.com/sdustinh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdustinh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdustinh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdustinh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdustinh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdustinh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdustinh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdustinh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdustinh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdustinh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":196053425,"node_id":"MDEzOkFzc2lnbmVkRXZlbnQxOTYwNTM0MjU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/events/196053425","actor":{"login":"lorenzo","id":37621,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NjIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37621?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo","html_url":"https://github.com/lorenzo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/gists{/gist_id}